    "revise": "You are the FIGURE REVISER (Opus) for \"The LLM Stack\". Chapter: content/14-capstone/09-post-training.md\nThe chapter's core intuitions: Post-training is a load-bearing LADDER: SFT (format/instinct) then DPO (taste) then narrow GRPO (a verifiable skill), each cheaper than the last and a rounding error against the pretraining bill, and each rung depends on the previous one -- skip SFT and DPO has nothing coherent to prefer; skip both and GRPO's reward is 0 everywhere and RL never starts.; Post-training changes what the model DOES (turn-taking, format, taste, one narrow skill), not fundamentally what it KNOWS: SFT and DPO reshape behavior already latent in the base model, and only RLVR adds capability -- and only inside a narrow, verifiable, in-distribution band.; Assistant-only loss masking: only assistant CONTENT tokens plus the closing <|end|> receive gradient (so the model learns to STOP); the system/user turns and the <|assistant|> role marker are context the model conditions on but is not trained to emit -- and the mask must land on the TARGET position after the causal shift, the single most common SFT bug.; DPO reshapes response log-probabilities RELATIVE to a frozen reference: push the winner up and the loser down; the intractable partition term appears in both and cancels in the difference (no reward model, no rollouts), and beta~0.1 is the KL leash -- with the notorious failure mode being BOTH rewards falling while the loss, which only sees the difference, still drops.\n\nReview each of these figures (the ones this chapter just drew/edited):\n  posttraining-ladder-100m, sft-assistant-mask-stackml, dpo-relative-reshaping, grpo-group-advantage-arith\n\nFor EACH: render and SEE it \u2014 `python3 scripts/preview_fig.py <NAME> --theme both` from /local-ssd/pk669/programming/llm-stack-textbook,\nthen view /tmp/figpreview/<NAME>.light.png and .dark.png. Judge strictly:\n  - Does it actually BUILD INTUITION for its concept (not just decorate)? Is it correct vs the chapter?\n  - Theme-safe (no hardcoded primary color; readable in BOTH light and dark)?\n  - Nothing clipped by the viewBox; no illegible overlaps; no tofu glyphs (ASCII only in the SVG)?\n  - Marker present in the chapter exactly once; figcaption has a bold lead + takeaway?\nIf a figure has ANY problem, FIX it: Edit /local-ssd/pk669/programming/llm-stack-textbook/figures/<NAME>.html (and re-render to confirm), or\nfix a missing/duplicate marker in the chapter. Re-verify after fixing.\n\nSet verdict per figure: good / fixed / still-broken / missing. `passed` = every figure good-or-fixed\nAND present. Return the structured object."
